(1-10, higher is better across all axes)

- cost: how easy it is on my subscription and wallet
- intelligence: soundness of its plans and implementations
- taste: ability to create a well-considered UI; a nicely balanced abstraction; prose that's pleasant to read
- cost is at most a tie-breaker; weight these in order of importance: intelligence > taste > cost

For subagents without a named profile, try to pick the right agent for the job. If it's not in the list, don't consider it. Also on the table: adversarial cross-lab reviews of your plans and implementations: OpenAI models reviewing Anthropic plans/implementations and vice versa.
